    {
      "kind": "narrative",
      "text": "For SFO to Bangkok on January 8, the trade-off is straightforward: prioritize a shorter overall trip in economy, or take the Turkish Airlines business-class award via Los Angeles and Istanbul. Both options add a separate SFO–LAX cash flight before the award journey.",
      "label": null,
      "reference_kind": null,
      "canonical_id": null,
      "journey": null,
      "component": null,
      "lead": null,
      "unavailable": false
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrative",
      "text": "The quicker option, “Economy via Istanbul,” leaves SFO at 2:05 p.m. and is listed at 110,000 Turkish miles. Its listed itinerary reaches Bangkok at 8:50 a.m. on January 10, after the LAX–Istanbul–Bangkok award routing. The separate positioning flight arrives at LAX at 3:46 p.m., leaving 2 hours 44 minutes before the award departure. That is the shortest complete journey in the supplied comparison, but it is still a long trip.",
      "label": null,
      "reference_kind": null,
